So I decided to try my hand at a set of symbols based on the old ones but modified to be more distinctive, conform more to the style of existing cast marks and make the I Ching reference more subtle, while retaining the basis in I Ching solstice/equinox symbolism:<br /> [There's supposed to be an image here but for some reason I'm having trouble uploading it. Giving up for now]<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/blob:http://forum.theonyxpath.com/4495060e-0a7f-4881-a037-a4bcf79c42fd\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The colour schemes are based on the description of the getimian animas as being black and white with bits of their caste colours mixed in, but you could also remove the black bits and change the white to the caste colours for sidereal-style cast-colour caste marks or change the caste-colour parts to white for solar/lunar style splat-colour caste marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}